<div class="card"><h2>Why Australians Choose China for Treatment</h2>
<ul><li><strong>Close and convenient:</strong> 8–10 hour flights from Sydney, Melbourne, and Brisbane to Guangzhou, Shanghai, and Beijing.</li><li><strong>30-day visa-free:</strong> Australian citizens enjoy 30-day visa-free entry (trial through 31 Dec 2026).</li><li><strong>English-speaking doctors:</strong> All recommended hospitals have international departments with fluent English staff.</li><li><strong>Short scheduling:</strong> Elective procedures are often scheduled within 2–4 weeks of consultation.</li><li><strong>JCI accreditation:</strong> Top Chinese hospitals meet the same standards as leading Australian private hospitals.</li></ul></div>

<div class="card"><h2>How We Help Australian Patients</h2><p><strong>Step 1:</strong> Tell us your condition, city preference, and budget — free, no commitment.</p><p><strong>Step 2:</strong> We match you with 2-3 hospitals and compare costs vs Australian private prices, with transport guidance.</p><p><strong>Step 3:</strong> We coordinate records, appointments, and airport pickup. You fly from Australia — we handle the rest.</p><p><strong>Cost:</strong> From $49 (hospital shortlist) to $399 (full journey management), with $149 verification in between. No hidden fees, no hospital commissions. <a href="pricing.html">See pricing →</a></p></div>

